.TH "RSYNC\-SSL\-TUNNEL" "1" "ftpsync Manual" ""
.SH NAME
rsync\-ssl\-tunnel \- Allows rsync to tunnel over TLS
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]rsync\-ssl\-tunnel\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]rsync\-ssl\-tunnel\f[R] is part of the ftpsync suite for mirroring
Debian and Debian\-like repositories of packages.
As there are way too many mirrors of Debian to populate them all from
the machine that generates the archive (\(lqftp\-master\(rq), mirrors
are organized in a tree\-shaped hierarchy.
Thus, every mirror has exactly one upstream from which it syncs, and
each mirror can have any number of downstreams which in turn sync from
it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-C\f[R]
The CA path for certificate verification
.RS
Default: \f[B]/etc/ssl/certs\f[R]
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-m\f[R]
The method used to connect to the remote host.
.RS
Default: \f[B]stunnel\f[R]
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-p\f[R]
The port used to connect to the remote host.
.RS
Default: \f[B]1873\f[R]
.RE
.SH EXAMPLE
Example use with rsync:
.PP
rsync \-e rsync\-ssl\-tunnel
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]ftpsync\f[R](1) +
